tion signals (14-20pp\\\\n      AUROC degradation), motivating our DIF-based approach which operates on behavioral\\\\n      patterns immune to NLL smoothing\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: 9a5bf5d3c7116cc4a104c06599fbcef2d1b5abf3\\\\n    title: On The Fragility of Benchmark Contamination Detection in Reasoning Models\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.02386\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2026\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n  white2025livebench:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - White, C.\\\\n    bibtex_key: white2025livebench\\\\n    category: benchmark_design\\\\n    doi: 10.48550/arXiv.2406.19314\\\\n    relevance: Monthly-updated contamination-free benchmark with objective scoring;\\\\n      no difficulty calibration or psychometric equivalence across updates\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: 4e5d86ea8eacd341d13123852d50d1ef62738744\\\\n    title: 'LiveBench: A Challenging, Contamination-Free LLM Benchmark'\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.19314\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2025\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n  zhang2024gsm1k:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Zhang, H.\\\\n    bibtex_key: zhang2024gsm1k\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: GSM1K documents 10-13% average accuracy drops from contamination; provides\\\\n      ground-truth contamination evidence and item-level effect sizes (delta 0.8-1.4\\\\n      logits) critical for our DIF power analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ef62f95c16f668f031d649799cbd79081c6d2b0f\\\\n    title: A Careful Examination of Large Language Model Performance on Grade School\\\\n      Arithmetic\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.00332\\\\n    venue: arXiv\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n  zhang2024minkpp: